    <statement><p>Which is a parametric equation for the curve <m>16 = \left(x-4\right)^{2}+\left(y+8\right)^{2}</m>?</p>
<p><var form="buttons">
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(4\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8,4+4\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(16\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8,4+16\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(4+4\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),4\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8\right)</m></p>
</li>
<li>
<p><m>c(t) = \left(4+16\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),16\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8\right)</m></p>
</li>
</var></p>
</statement>
    <solution><m>(4, -8)</m>.  Using the parametric representation of a circle we get <m>c(t) = \left(4+4\cos\mathopen{}\left(t\right),4\sin\mathopen{}\left(t\right)-8\right)</m>.


</solution>
